# Recipe export and import (API.md §4, §8). Sign in first with dev-login (Development only); the cookie is kept between requests.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5106/api/v1
@recipeId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Sign in (dev-login)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/dev-login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: fetch

{ "email": "ania@test.local", "nickname": "ania" }

### Export a recipe you can see, with the variants you can see (404 when not visible)
GET {{baseUrl}}/recipes/{{recipeId}}/export

### Import the sample file: creates a private recipe and private variants owned by you
### (400 import.invalid_format, 400 import.unsupported_version, 413 import.too_large, 429 rate_limited)
POST {{baseUrl}}/recipes/import
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: fetch

< ../../shared/samples/export-v1.json

### Recipes the sample file could become variants of: visible, non-archived, same normalized title (own first, then newest; at most 10)
GET {{baseUrl}}/recipes/import-matches?title=Nale%C5%9Bniki

### Import the sample file as variants of a recipe: "Wersja @<author>" plus one variant per file variant
### (201 when something was created, 200 when everything was skipped; 404 recipe.not_found, 409 recipe.archived)
POST {{baseUrl}}/recipes/{{recipeId}}/variants/import
Content-Type: application/json
X-Requested-With: fetch

< ../../shared/samples/export-v1.json
